# Rust Async I/O Timeout Requirement

**CLAUDE-001**: All Rust async functions that perform external I/O operations must have explicit timeouts set. This includes network requests, file operations, database queries, and any blocking operations that wait for external resources.

```rust
// Example of compliant code
async fn fetch_data_with_timeout() -> Result<String, Error> {
    tokio::time::timeout(
        Duration::from_secs(30),
        fetch_data()
    ).await?
}
```

Timeouts prevent hanging operations from blocking indefinitely and ensure system responsiveness. Use `tokio::time::timeout()` or similar mechanisms. Set reasonable timeout values based on expected operation duration. This rule applies to all external dependencies including HTTP clients, database connections, and file I/O operations.
